> [The] use of the torture by the CIA post-9/11 has been[ revealed] by one of its former agents, Glenn Car[le]. In 2002, Carle was tasked with interrogating a suspected high level al-Qaeda member using so-called enhanced interrogation techniques. But when he found the suspect was the wrong man, he found[ himself] in the difficult position of criticising the value of a high profile CIA case and the institute’s use of torture.[][][][][][][][][]

